{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"a8f1a005-6197-4ac8-b6c3-3f7619cec3c7","agentId":"a2dfaa35dbefe2a3a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Audit Phase 3C 路线图 P1 #24：Cache-aware user-layer pack 5 件套（THP madvise + tcmalloc/jemalloc LD_PRELOAD + PGO build + L3 cache isolation + AMO aggregation），claim \"+15-30% combined for long-running 168h workloads\"。\n\n## 项目背景\n\n终末地工业规划器 70×70 网格 266 设施 exact LBBD 求解器，CP-SAT-based。168h campaign 是 long-running compute-heavy workload。硬件：i9-13900KS 24T HT-off, DDR5-7600 48GB, CachyOS Linux (kernel 7.0.5-2-cachyos with BORE/EEVDF scheduler).\n\n## 原始 claim\n\n- 路线图 (`/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd/docs/phase3c_optimization_roadmap_v1.md`) 第 58 行：\n  > | 24 | **Cache-aware user-layer pack: THP + tcmalloc/jemalloc + PGO + L3 isolation + AMO aggregation** | R11 `ae3590b7e2f938057` | +15-30% combined for long-running 168h workloads | THP/malloc swap ~½ day; PGO ~2-3 days; L3 isolation 1 hour | ~10× |\n- 来源 transcript: `/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd/docs/research/agent_transcripts/ae3590b7e2f938057.output`\n\n## Audit 任务（按顺序）\n\n1. **Read R11 transcript** (`ae3590b7e2f938057.output`) 找 #24 那段 + 5 件套各自宣称的 individual ROI（如果有）+ 数字源头。\n\n2. **每件套 individual 核实**：\n\n   a. **THP (Transparent Huge Pages) madvise**: WebSearch 找 OR-Tools / CP-SAT / SAT solver 上 THP 的 benchmark 数据。CP-SAT 是不是 large-heap workload（168h 跑 ~24-40 GiB RSS）？THP madvise vs always 区别？\n   \n   b. **tcmalloc / jemalloc LD_PRELOAD**: WebSearch 找 Python C-extension（OR-Tools 是 C++ 通过 swig 包装）+ tcmalloc/jemalloc 的 benchmark。对 CP-SAT 这种主要在 C++ 层 alloc 的工作负载，LD_PRELOAD 收益典型多大？\n   \n   c. **PGO (Profile-Guided Optimization) build**: 重点查 OR-Tools 自己有没有官方 PGO build option（看 ortools/Makefile 或 BUILD.bazel）。如果没有，要从源码 rebuild 加 PGO 真实工作量是 \"2-3 days\" 还是更多？OR-Tools 官方提供的 manylinux wheel 已经是怎么编的？\n   \n   d. **L3 cache isolation (cgroups v2 / cpuset)**: 通过 systemd-run --scope --cpuset-cpus 限定核心 + L3 cache occupancy / Intel CAT (Cache Allocation Technology)。 i9-13900KS 36MB L3 cache 在 CP-SAT 24 thread 工作负载下是 cache-bound 还是 compute-bound？\n   \n   e. **AMO aggregation**: 这是什么？AMO = atomic memory operations? at-most-one constraint aggregation? Affordable Memory Operations? 不要凭名字猜——看 transcript 怎么说的，再用 WebSearch / OR-Tools docs verify。\n\n3. **加和是否 plausible**: THP / malloc / L3 isolation 都是 cache locality 类干预，容易 **double-count** 同一份 cache locality benefit。15-30% combined 是不是把 5 件 each ~5% 简单加和？\n\n4. **真实 168h 长跑 combined gain 估**：基于 1-3 步发现，估真实可达 combined gain（vs claim 的 15-30%）。哪几件最值得做？\n\n## 输出格式（不超过 700 字，中文 OK）\n\n```\n## 1. claim 出处\n[transcript 里 #24 那段 + 5 件套 individual claim 数字]\n\n## 2. THP madvise 核实\n[一段：典型 SAT/CP solver benchmark + 我们工作负载契合度]\n\n## 3. tcmalloc/jemalloc 核实\n[一段]\n\n## 4. PGO 核实\n[一段：OR-Tools 默认 wheel 编译选项 + rebuild 真实成本]\n\n## 5. L3 isolation 核实\n[一段：i9-13900KS 36MB L3 + CP-SAT 是否 cache-bound]\n\n## 6. AMO aggregation 核实\n[一段：先确认 AMO 具体指什么，再估值]\n\n## 7. combined 加和合理性\n[一段：double-count 风险]\n\n## verdict\nGO / GO-WITH-CAVEATS / PARTIALLY_REFUTED / REFUTED\n[3-4 行：哪几件值得做、修正后的 combined gain、剔除哪些]\n```\n\n## 操作准则\n\n- 必须 read transcript 文件\n- 必须用 WebSearch / WebFetch 找 OR-Tools 官方 build doc 或 SAT solver benchmark paper\n- 不要凭训练数据估，要 URL / file:line 引用\n- 保持简洁\n\n开始。"},"uuid":"a02bfac6-1af3-4e95-a493-abe6cde4c50e","timestamp":"2026-05-09T18:02:20.064Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"a02bfac6-1af3-4e95-a493-abe6cde4c50e","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a2dfaa35dbefe2a3a","attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_delta","addedNames":["CronCreate","CronDelete","CronList","EnterWorktree","ExitWorktree","Monitor","NotebookEdit","PushNotification","RemoteTrigger","TaskCreate","TaskGet","TaskList","TaskStop","TaskUpdate","WebFetch","WebSearch"],"addedLines":["CronCreate","CronDelete","CronList","EnterWorktree","ExitWorktree","Monitor","NotebookEdit","PushNotification","RemoteTrigger","TaskCreate","TaskGet","TaskList","TaskStop","TaskUpdate","WebFetch","WebSearch"],"removedNames":[],"readdedNames":[]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"1f836c97-bc11-4fca-b041-8c72c06cd4dc","timestamp":"2026-05-09T18:02:20.070Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"1f836c97-bc11-4fca-b041-8c72c06cd4dc","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a2dfaa35dbefe2a3a","attachment":{"type":"skill_listing","content":"- update-config: Use this skill to configure the Claude Code harness via settings.json. Automated behaviors (\"from now on when X\", \"each time X\", \"whenever X\", \"before/after X\") require hooks configured in settings.json - the harness executes these, not Claude, so memory/preferences cannot fulfill them. Also use for: permissions (\"allow X\", \"add permission\", \"move permission to\"), env vars (\"set X=Y\"), hook troubleshooting, or any changes to settings.json/settings.local.json files. Examples: \"allow npm commands\", \"add bq permission to global settings\", \"move permission to user settings\", \"set DEBUG=true\", \"when claude stops show X\". For simple settings like theme/model, suggest the /config command.\n- keybindings-help: Use when the user wants to customize keyboard shortcuts, rebind keys, add chord bindings, or modify ~/.claude/keybindings.json. Examples: \"rebind ctrl+s\", \"add a chord shortcut\", \"change the submit key\", \"customize keybindings\".\n- simplify: Review changed code for reuse, quality, and efficiency, then fix any issues found.\n- fewer-permission-prompts: Scan your transcripts for common read-only Bash and MCP tool calls, then add a prioritized allowlist to project .claude/settings.json to reduce permission prompts.\n- loop: Run a prompt or slash command on a recurring interval (e.g. /loop 5m /foo). Omit the interval to let the model self-pace. - When the user wants to set up a recurring task, poll for status, or run something repeatedly on an interval (e.g. \"check the deploy every 5 minutes\", \"keep running /babysit-prs\"). Do NOT invoke for one-off tasks.\n- schedule: Create, update, list, or run scheduled remote agents (routines) that execute on a cron schedule. - When the user wants to schedule a recurring remote agent, set up automated tasks, create a cron job for Claude Code, or manage their scheduled agents/routines. Also use when the user wants a one-time scheduled run (\"run this once at 3pm\", \"remind me to check X tomorrow\").\n- claude-api: Build, debug, and optimize Claude API / Anthropic SDK apps. Apps built with this skill should include prompt caching. Also handles migrating existing Claude API code between Claude model versions (4.5 → 4.6, 4.6 → 4.7, retired-model replacements).\nTRIGGER when: code imports `anthropic`/`@anthropic-ai/sdk`; user asks for the Claude API, Anthropic SDK, or Managed Agents; user adds/modifies/tunes a Claude feature (caching, thinking, compaction, tool use, batch, files, citations, memory) or model (Opus/Sonnet/Haiku) in a file; questions about prompt caching / cache hit rate in an Anthropic SDK project.\nSKIP: file imports `openai`/other-provider SDK, filename like `*-openai.py`/`*-generic.py`, provider-neutral code, general programming/ML.\n- init: Initialize a new CLAUDE.md file with codebase documentation\n- review: Review a pull request\n- security-review: Complete a security review of the pending changes on the current branch","skillCount":10,"isInitial":true},"type":"attachment","uuid":"711f52ce-e5ec-4dff-acad-fbb7a7235c02","timestamp":"2026-05-09T18:02:20.071Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
