{"parentUuid":"6e1c41ee-c6d9-4e2e-a184-3c480e197b94","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a2dfaa35dbefe2a3a","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01CfwX4yNw8LSkhn1n9VthvS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QCaiEGzmn5ZptW8jqoBEZp","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"jemalloc tcmalloc LD_PRELOAD Python C extension benchmark CP-SAT solver"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4819,"cache_read_input_tokens":28489,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4819,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CasSArRTsxvjqtNxztNzM","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"e8919a76-57ee-45ee-abb6-04986f3c0df5","timestamp":"2026-05-09T18:02:59.969Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e8919a76-57ee-45ee-abb6-04986f3c0df5","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"a8f1a005-6197-4ac8-b6c3-3f7619cec3c7","agentId":"a2dfaa35dbefe2a3a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QCaiEGzmn5ZptW8jqoBEZp","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"jemalloc tcmalloc LD_PRELOAD Python C extension benchmark CP-SAT solver\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Performance Tuning Guide — intel_extension_for_pytorch 1.13.100+cpu documentation\",\"url\":\"https://intel.github.io/intel-extension-for-pytorch/cpu/1.13.100+cpu/tutorials/performance_tuning/tuning_guide.html\"},{\"title\":\"Testing Memory Allocators: ptmalloc2 vs. tcmalloc vs. hoard vs. jemalloc | Hacker News\",\"url\":\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=17457699\"},{\"title\":\"libmalloc, jemalloc, tcmalloc, mimalloc - Exploring Different Memory Allocators - DEV Community\",\"url\":\"https://dev.to/frosnerd/libmalloc-jemalloc-tcmalloc-mimalloc-exploring-different-memory-allocators-4lp3\"},{\"title\":\"Very high virtual memory consumption and slow performance · Issue #285 · google/tcmalloc\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/tcmalloc/issues/285\"},{\"title\":\"Testing Memory Allocators: ptmalloc2 vs tcmalloc vs hoard vs jemalloc While Trying to Simulate Real-World Loads - IT Hare on Soft.ware\",\"url\":\"http://ithare.com/testing-memory-allocators-ptmalloc2-tcmalloc-hoard-jemalloc-while-trying-to-simulate-real-world-loads/\"},{\"title\":\"jemalloc vs malloc vs tcmalloc: Why Your Server's Default Allocator Is Killing P99 Latency - DEV Community\",\"url\":\"https://dev.to/kunal_d6a8fea2309e1571ee7/jemalloc-vs-malloc-vs-tcmalloc-why-your-servers-default-allocator-is-killing-p99-latency-6l8\"},{\"title\":\"Benchmarking Ruby's Heap: malloc, tcmalloc, jemalloc — Engineering Blog\",\"url\":\"https://engineering.appfolio.com/appfolio-engineering/2018/2/1/benchmarking-rubys-heap-malloc-tcmalloc-jemalloc\"},{\"title\":\"Selecting a malloc variant between default, mimalloc, jemalloc, rpmalloc\",\"url\":\"https://docs.bell-sw.com/alpaquita-linux/latest/how-to/malloc/\"},{\"title\":\"Small Datum: Battle of the Mallocators\",\"url\":\"http://smalldatum.blogspot.com/2025/04/battle-of-mallocators.html\"},{\"title\":\"Getting Started · jemalloc/jemalloc Wiki · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/jemalloc/jemalloc/wiki/Getting-Started\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found information about using jemalloc and tcmalloc with LD_PRELOAD for performance optimization. However, the results don't contain specific information about CP-SAT solver benchmarks with Python C extensions. Here's what I found:\n\n## Using jemalloc/tcmalloc with LD_PRELOAD\n\nAdding the path of Jemalloc/TCMalloc dynamic library to the LD_PRELOAD environment variable allows you to switch memory allocators. The typical usage is:\n\n```\nLD_PRELOAD=<jemalloc.so/tcmalloc.so>:$LD_PRELOAD\n```\n\nUsing LD_PRELOAD to inject jemalloc at runtime works if your application does not statically link a malloc implementation.\n\n## Performance Characteristics\n\nFor the large majority of server workloads on Linux, jemalloc or tcmalloc is probably the right choice of allocator. In comparative benchmarks:\n\n- One benchmark showed about an 11% speedup with jemalloc, and between 3% and 10% speedup with tcmalloc\n- jemalloc, mimalloc, and tcmalloc manage to keep overhead below 30% for most allocation sizes\n\n## Important Caveat\n\nYou should not mix allocators - if you LD_PRELOAD jemalloc but some shared library statically links its own allocator, you'll have a bad time.\n\nHowever, the search results don't contain specific benchmarks comparing these allocators with the OR-Tools CP-SAT solver or Python C extensions. You may need to conduct your own benchmarks for that specific use case.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"1f36f6cd-78a1-46be-8cfa-6ce1fa29be70","timestamp":"2026-05-09T18:03:06.678Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e8919a76-57ee-45ee-abb6-04986f3c0df5","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"6e1c41ee-c6d9-4e2e-a184-3c480e197b94","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"a8f1a005-6197-4ac8-b6c3-3f7619cec3c7","agentId":"a2dfaa35dbefe2a3a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AiUdybzgyxem4SZ5aLWNim","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools CP-SAT PGO profile-guided optimization build wheel manylinux\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Release Notes | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/support/release_notes\"},{\"title\":\"Add official Python 3.14 wheels (Linux/macOS/Windows) for OR-Tools · Issue #4859 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/4859\"},{\"title\":\"[v9] pgo: add clang's Profile Guided Optimization infrastructure - Patchwork\",\"url\":\"https://patchwork.kernel.org/project/linux-kbuild/patch/20210407211704.367039-1-morbo@google.com/\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"},{\"title\":\"Evaluate using Profile-Guided Optimization (PGO) and Post-Link Optimization (PLO) · google/or-tools · Discussion #4012\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/4012\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"Profile-Guided Optimization - Ubuntu Server documentation\",\"url\":\"https://ubuntu.com/server/docs/explanation/performance/perf-pgo/\"},{\"title\":\"How to Use Profile-Guided Optimization (PGO) on Ubuntu\",\"url\":\"https://oneuptime.com/blog/post/2026-03-02-profile-guided-optimization-pgo-ubuntu/view\"},{\"title\":\"Proposal: profile-guided optimization\",\"url\":\"https://go.googlesource.com/proposal/+/master/design/55022-pgo.md\"},{\"title\":\"ortools · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/ortools/\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here's what I found about OR-Tools, CP-SAT, PGO, and manylinux:\n\n## OR-Tools and Manylinux Wheels\n\nPyPI modules on Linux platforms are now delivered as wheel files using the manylinux1 tag. Currently, OR-Tools wheels are available for multiple Python versions (3.10-3.14) with manylinux tags for both x86-64 and aarch64 architectures.\n\n## PGO Discussion for OR-Tools\n\nThere is an active discussion about applying Profile-Guided Optimization to OR-Tools. Profile-Guided Optimization (PGO) and Post-Link Optimization (PLO) improvements have been evaluated on multiple projects with networking apps, databases, and runtimes showing performance benefits, and it's been suggested that optimizing OR-Tools with PGO could be a good idea.\n\nHowever, PGO optimizations require a training dataset which is not part of OR-Tools, so this should ideally be done at the application level when linking the final binary, particularly for C++. You can build a PGO-optimized version of OR-Tools for Python since PGO works not only for applications but also for libraries.\n\n## CP-SAT Performance\n\nThe CP-SAT solver has received significant improvements, including API changes, performance enhancements, and expanded functionality for constraints and linear expressions.\n\nThe search results indicate that while PGO optimization for OR-Tools has been discussed, it's not currently implemented in the official build process. Users interested in PGO optimization would need to build OR-Tools from source with appropriate PGO compiler flags.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"d9b52afa-fed9-4517-ac74-933b6a2f3d6f","timestamp":"2026-05-09T18:03:06.729Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6e1c41ee-c6d9-4e2e-a184-3c480e197b94","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
