{"parentUuid":"307958a5-3df1-4221-bba5-f43bb2a80b88","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a2dfaa35dbefe2a3a","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01MjiiuedfvZvv8kKtbtegxK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018fSYteDeuY1jVFWBzSAdZ4","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"transparent huge pages SAT CP-SAT solver benchmark TLB miss"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4679,"cache_read_input_tokens":33308,"output_tokens":357,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4679},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":357,"cache_read_input_tokens":33308,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4679,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4679,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CasSBqZQEgXHPeoVvhuHW","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"a57636a4-7946-4a87-82c5-f86e4ffa321d","timestamp":"2026-05-09T18:03:14.864Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"983ada03-2e1d-4253-8c87-94b1cd2695af","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"a8f1a005-6197-4ac8-b6c3-3f7619cec3c7","agentId":"a2dfaa35dbefe2a3a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ACC1YGNZqxok3qyeSHZc6A","type":"tool_result","content":"# OR-Tools PGO and Optimization Status\n\nBased on the GitHub discussion, here's what we know:\n\n**Official PGO Wheels:**\nNo, the OR-Tools team does not currently build official wheels with PGO optimization.\n\n**Benchmark Numbers:**\nThe maintainer indicates there are no published benchmark numbers for PGO on CP-SAT. When asked about PGO implementation, the team lead stated: \"they can provide a few % speedup, while improving CP-SAT can bring exponential gain. So I should not spend my time on it.\"\n\n**Official Build Flags:**\nThe discussion does not specify what flags are used in the official manylinux wheels.\n\n**Key Context:**\nThe maintainer acknowledged that PGO could help performance but cited resource constraints and prioritization toward algorithmic improvements over compilation optimizations. The team remains open to community contributions in this area, noting that \"PR welcome\" for those interested in implementing PGO support."}]},"uuid":"3f0c4850-4875-4ef0-a659-edcb461a421a","timestamp":"2026-05-09T18:03:18.902Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"983ada03-2e1d-4253-8c87-94b1cd2695af","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"307958a5-3df1-4221-bba5-f43bb2a80b88","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"a8f1a005-6197-4ac8-b6c3-3f7619cec3c7","agentId":"a2dfaa35dbefe2a3a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Py9kPC9xMAotgRCrVckaq2","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Intel CAT L3 cache allocation technology i9-13900 SAT solver cache-bound benchmark\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Intel® Core™ i9-13900K Processor (36M Cache, up to 5.80 GHz) - Product Specifications | Intel\",\"url\":\"https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/products/sku/230496/intel-core-i913900k-processor-36m-cache-up-to-5-80-ghz/specifications.html\"},{\"title\":\"Intel® Core™ i9-13900 Processor (36M Cache, up to 5.60 GHz) - Product Specifications | Intel\",\"url\":\"https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/products/sku/230499/intel-core-i913900-processor-36m-cache-up-to-5-60-ghz/specifications.html\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction to Cache Allocation Technology in the Intel® Xeon® Processor E5 v4 Family\",\"url\":\"https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/developer/articles/technical/introduction-to-cache-allocation-technology.html\"},{\"title\":\"Intel RDT for 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-13900KS · Issue #249 · intel/intel-cmt-cat\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/intel/intel-cmt-cat/issues/249\"},{\"title\":\"Intel® Resource Director Technology (Intel® RDT) — ECI documentation\",\"url\":\"https://eci.intel.com/docs/3.3/development/performance/intel-pqos.html\"},{\"title\":\"Intel Cache Allocation Technology and Code and Data Prioritization Features\",\"url\":\"https://xenbits.xenproject.org/docs/unstable/features/intel_psr_cat_cdp.html\"},{\"title\":\"Intel's i9-13900K CPU has been spotted with 68MB of Cache\",\"url\":\"https://overclock3d.net/news/cpu_mainboard/ryzen_watch_out_-_intel_s_i9-13900k_cpu_has_been_spotted_with_68mb_of_cache/1\"},{\"title\":\"Alleged Intel Raptor Lake Core i9-13900 CPU With 24 Cores & 32 Threads Spotted: 3.8 GHz Clocks, 36 MB L3 Cache & 65W TDP\",\"url\":\"https://wccftech.com/alleged-intel-raptor-lake-core-i9-13900-cpu-with-24-cores-32-threads-spotted-3-8-ghz-clocks-36-mb-l3-cache-65w-tdp/\"},{\"title\":\"Alleged Intel 13th Gen Core i9-13900K Raptor Lake Leak Confirms Chunky Cache Upgrade | HotHardware\",\"url\":\"https://hothardware.com/news/alleged-intel-13th-gen-core-i9-13900k-raptor-lake-leak-confirms-chunky-cache-upgrade\"},{\"title\":\"Usage Models for Cache Allocation Technology in the Intel® Xeon® Processor E5 v4 Family\",\"url\":\"https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/developer/articles/technical/cache-allocation-technology-usage-models.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found:\n\n## Intel CAT (Cache Allocation Technology)\n\nIntel Cache Allocation Technology (CAT) provides a method to partition processor caches and assign these partitions to a Class-of-Service (COS), and associating workloads to different COS can effectively isolate parts of cache available to a workload, thus preventing cache contention altogether.\n\nCAT allows an OS or hypervisor to control allocation of a CPU's shared cache based on application/domain priority or Class of Service (COS), with each COS configured using capacity bitmasks (CBMs) which represent cache capacity and indicate the degree of overlap and isolation between classes.\n\n## Intel i9-13900 Cache Specifications\n\nThe Intel Core i9-13900 Processor features 36M Cache and runs up to 5.60 GHz.\n\n## Regarding CAT Support on 13th Gen i9\n\nAccording to technical discussions found in the search results, there appear to be some limitations with L3 CAT support detection on 13th Gen Intel Core i9 processors, though the underlying L3 cache infrastructure is present. However, the search results did not contain specific information about SAT solver benchmarks or cache-bound benchmark performance comparisons with CAT enabled on the i9-13900.\n\nIf you're looking for specific benchmark data comparing SAT solver performance with and without CAT optimizations on the i9-13900, you may need to search for academic papers or specialized performance benchmarks, as this information was not available in the general web sources returned.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"85f23f95-28cf-43a0-8c93-8653ce59f6b2","timestamp":"2026-05-09T18:03:21.662Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"307958a5-3df1-4221-bba5-f43bb2a80b88","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"a57636a4-7946-4a87-82c5-f86e4ffa321d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"a8f1a005-6197-4ac8-b6c3-3f7619cec3c7","agentId":"a2dfaa35dbefe2a3a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018fSYteDeuY1jVFWBzSAdZ4","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"transparent huge pages SAT CP-SAT solver benchmark TLB miss\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Transparent Hugepages: measuring the performance impact - The mole is digging\",\"url\":\"https://alexandrnikitin.github.io/blog/transparent-hugepages-measuring-the-performance-impact/\"},{\"title\":\"Transparent Hugepage Support — The Linux Kernel documentation\",\"url\":\"https://docs.kernel.org/admin-guide/mm/transhuge.html\"},{\"title\":\"Towards Faster Reasoners by Using Transparent Huge Pages | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/344179418_Towards_Faster_Reasoners_by_Using_Transparent_Huge_Pages\"},{\"title\":\"Towards Faster Reasoners by Using Transparent Huge Pages | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-58475-7_18\"},{\"title\":\"Transparent Hugepage Support — The Linux Kernel documentation\",\"url\":\"https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/v5.4/admin-guide/mm/transhuge.html\"},{\"title\":\"Examining Huge Pages or Transparent Huge Pages performance | Red Hat Developer\",\"url\":\"https://developers.redhat.com/blog/2014/03/10/examining-huge-pages-or-transparent-huge-pages-performance\"},{\"title\":\"JVM Anatomy Quark #2: Transparent Huge Pages\",\"url\":\"https://shipilev.net/jvm/anatomy-quarks/2-transparent-huge-pages/\"},{\"title\":\"Advanced Page Table Management and Transparent Huge Pages (THP) Internals\",\"url\":\"https://howtech.substack.com/p/advanced-page-table-management-and\"},{\"title\":\"Huge pages part 5: A deeper look at TLBs and costs [LWN.net]\",\"url\":\"https://lwn.net/Articles/379748/\"},{\"title\":\"Transparent Huge Pages (THP): Reducing TLB Pressure | Abhik Sarkar\",\"url\":\"https://www.abhik.ai/concepts/memory/transparent-huge-pages\"}]\n\nI've completed the web search for \"transparent huge pages SAT CP-SAT solver benchmark TLB miss\". Here's a summary of the search results:\n\n## Key Findings\n\nThe search results reveal relevant research on how Transparent Huge Pages (THP) can improve SAT solver performance:\n\n**SAT Solver Optimization Research:**\nResearch on using transparent huge pages with SAT solvers shows an average speedup of 60% on benchmarks, with improvements also applied to MiniSAT2.0 achieving a 20% runtime improvement on average. The analysis was performed on a CDCL-based SAT solver using a subset of the industrial SAT Competition 2009 benchmark.\n\n**TLB Miss and Performance:**\nSuperpages (used by Transparent Huge Pages) enable each TLB entry to map a large physical memory region into virtual address space, which dramatically increases TLB coverage and reduces TLB misses.\n\n**General THP Benefits:**\nTransparent Hugepage Support manages large pages automatically and transparently for applications, reducing the number of TLB misses and making page table walking cheaper.\n\nThe search results include academic papers from Springer on \"Towards Faster Reasoners by Using Transparent Huge Pages,\" indicating this is an active research area combining system-level optimizations with solver performance.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"d3f2e4f7-49da-4f3c-8b47-86f897b730e9","timestamp":"2026-05-09T18:03:21.819Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a57636a4-7946-4a87-82c5-f86e4ffa321d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d3f2e4f7-49da-4f3c-8b47-86f897b730e9","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a2dfaa35dbefe2a3a","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01V5e7YYCKYRXR5YWPwH9PbG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent. THP claim is well-supported (avg 60% on reasoners, 20% on MiniSAT). PGO confirmed not in official wheels and team thinks it's \"few %\". Let me check one last thing — what AMO aggregation could mean in CP-SAT context:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3611,"cache_read_input_tokens":37987,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3611,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CasSCx3c8EG8htHa7qW51","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"861f089e-3cd1-42b3-8d51-a749647555b3","timestamp":"2026-05-09T18:03:27.240Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
