{"parentUuid":"bb657dd4-ddc0-4b76-882e-2923eaf5785b","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a2dfaa35dbefe2a3a","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01V5e7YYCKYRXR5YWPwH9PbG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XCwNGEyQVg8o18TB2e6P1m","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"grep -rn \"AMO\\|at-most-one\\|at_most_one\" /home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd/docs/phase3c_optimization_roadmap_v1.md | head -20","description":"Search roadmap for AMO context"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3611,"cache_read_input_tokens":37987,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3611,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CasSCx3c8EG8htHa7qW51","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"0392df06-cde0-4878-9ab6-f47dc389f36c","timestamp":"2026-05-09T18:03:29.071Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"0392df06-cde0-4878-9ab6-f47dc389f36c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"a8f1a005-6197-4ac8-b6c3-3f7619cec3c7","agentId":"a2dfaa35dbefe2a3a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XCwNGEyQVg8o18TB2e6P1m","type":"tool_result","content":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd/docs/phase3c_optimization_roadmap_v1.md:58:| 24 | **Cache-aware user-layer pack: THP + tcmalloc/jemalloc + PGO + L3 isolation + AMO aggregation** | R11 `ae3590b7e2f938057` | +15-30% combined for long-running 168h workloads | THP/malloc swap ~½ day; PGO ~2-3 days; L3 isolation 1 hour | ~10× |","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"69430e36-28ed-4cf4-8c19-f7e16df3fd26","timestamp":"2026-05-09T18:03:29.085Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0392df06-cde0-4878-9ab6-f47dc389f36c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"bb657dd4-ddc0-4b76-882e-2923eaf5785b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"a8f1a005-6197-4ac8-b6c3-3f7619cec3c7","agentId":"a2dfaa35dbefe2a3a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BXpznW7MXpkxmzeZPZmu8k","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"at-most-one\" AMO aggregation CP-SAT OR-Tools constraint propagator\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"A New Method to Encode the At-Most-One Constraint into SAT | Proceedings of the 6th International Symposium on Information and Communication Technology\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/2833258.2833293\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Rostering: Complete Guide to Constraint Programming for Workforce Scheduling - Interactive | Michael Brenndoerfer | Michael Brenndoerfer\",\"url\":\"https://mbrenndoerfer.com/writing/cp-sat-rostering-constraint-programming-workforce-scheduling\"},{\"title\":\"Selecting SAT Encodings for Pseudo-Boolean and Linear Integer Constraints\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol235-cp2022/LIPIcs.CP.2022.38/LIPIcs.CP.2022.38.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-Bench: Evaluating Large Language Models for Constraint Modelling\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2506.06052v1\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT, UNKNOWN status with complete solution hint · Issue #3750 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3750\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT get's stuck when trying to maximize sum of boolean variables that are all added as assumptions · google/or-tools · Discussion #3630\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3630\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) A New Method to Encode the At-Most-One Constraint into SAT\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/301455290_A_New_Method_to_Encode_the_At-Most-One_Constraint_into_SAT\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about at-most-one (AMO) constraints and their use in CP-SAT and OR-Tools.\n\n## Key Findings\n\n**At-Most-One Constraint Definition:**\nThe at-most-one (AMO) constraint is one of the most widely used constraints during the process of translating a practical problem into a propositional satisfiability (SAT) instance.\n\n**CP-SAT Implementation:**\nThe search results show that CP-SAT includes specific handling for AMO constraints. In CP-SAT's presolve phase, there is a MaxClique operation that merges constraints into at_most_ones, and the presolve rules include \"setppc: bool_or in at_most_one\" transformations.\n\n**AMO Aggregation and Encoding:**\nAMO sets can come from an integer variable or are detected automatically. Additionally, when an integer variable with a domain larger than 2 appears in a linear constraint, it is replaced with an AMO group of terms representing each value except the smallest.\n\n**Constraint Propagation:**\nWhen the solver sets one variable, it can immediately infer consequences for related variables through constraint propagation. Research shows that most encodings of the at-most-one constraint are 2-CNFs and achieve propagation completeness.\n\nThe search results indicate that CP-SAT uses sophisticated preprocessing to detect and aggregate AMO constraints, which helps improve solver efficiency through better constraint propagation during the solving process.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"e7f0c062-7fba-4905-9b7d-53dc5dcb68c4","timestamp":"2026-05-09T18:03:36.124Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bb657dd4-ddc0-4b76-882e-2923eaf5785b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e7f0c062-7fba-4905-9b7d-53dc5dcb68c4","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a2dfaa35dbefe2a3a","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01RpCA9htNAZkgeAP6eQ6Wdd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have everything I need. Now to deliver the audit verdict.\n\n## 1. claim 出处\n\nTranscript R11 (`ae3590b7e2f938057.output`, line 52) 末尾\"对 CP-SAT 用户层（不改 OR-Tools 源码）能做的\"列了 7 条，含 individual 数字：\n- THP + tcmalloc/jemalloc：**1-5%**（合并算一项）\n- march+LTO+PGO 三件套：**10-20%**（已被路线图 P1 #13 单独列出）\n- NUMA / CPU pinning + L3 隔离：无单独数字\n- worker matrix（boolean_encoding_level 等）、并发数控制、AI sidecar ordering：无单独数字\n- 末句：\"仅靠用户层（含 PGO）叠加 15-30%\"\n\n**关键发现**：transcript 里**完全没有 \"AMO aggregation\"** 这一条，路线图把它塞进 #24 是无源插入。最接近的相关材料是第 3 节里 \"Compact-Table 已是 OR-Tools 默认 table propagator\"，跟用户层 AMO 没关系。\n\n## 2. THP madvise 核实\n\n最强证据。Springer 2020 *Towards Faster Reasoners by Using THP*：在 CDCL SAT solver 上 **平均 60% 提速**，MiniSAT2.0 +20%。Linux kernel docs 确认 THP 削减 TLB miss + 廉化 page-walk。我们 168h 长跑 RSS 24-40 GiB 是典型 large-heap 工作负载，完全契合。**transcript 给的 1-5% 太保守**，更可能 +10-25%。建议 `madvise` 而非 `always`（避免 fork 时 latency spike）。\n\n## 3. tcmalloc/jemalloc LD_PRELOAD 核实\n\nHacker News / Bell-SW / DEV 多组 benchmark 一致：服务器工作负载典型 **+3-11%**（jemalloc 11%, tcmalloc 3-10%）。OR-Tools wheel 是 manylinux .so，不静态链 malloc，`LD_PRELOAD` 可生效。CP-SAT 在 C++ 层频繁分配 clause/conflict 结构，多线程 contention 是 ptmalloc 弱项 → 落到 +5-10% 区间。**transcript 把 THP+malloc 合并算 1-5% 偏低**。\n\n## 4. PGO 核实\n\nOR-Tools GitHub Discussion #4012 ([链接](https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/4012)) Perron 团队明确：**官方 wheel 不做 PGO**，团队认为\"PGO can provide a few % speedup, while improving CP-SAT can bring exponential gain\"。意味着：(a) 自己 rebuild 收益空间真的存在；(b) Perron 自己估的 few% 远低于 transcript 里 R6 引用的 +5-10%；(c) 工作量 transcript 的 \"2-3 days\" 严重低估——OR-Tools 从源码 build 涉及 abseil/protobuf/scip/highs 一堆依赖，初次 +PGO instrumented build + 8-24h 采样 + 重 build + 测试，**实际 5-7 天**。awesome-pgo 大量 +10% 实例不是 SAT solver——SAT solver 已经被 layout 优化过，边际收益更低。**修正：+3-7%, 5-7 天**。\n\n## 5. L3 isolation 核实\n\ni9-13900KS 36MB L3 / 24T = 1.5MB/thread。CDCL 经典数据：60-70% runtime 等内存（transcript §1）→ 是 cache-bound。但 Intel CAT (RDT) 在 13th gen consumer i9 **支持有限**（[intel-cmt-cat issue #249](https://github.com/intel/intel-cmt-cat/issues/249)）— L3 CAT 主要在 Xeon。可做的真正干预是 **cgroups v2 cpuset 把 worker 钉 P-core**（已在 CLAUDE.md cachyos_setup.sh 路径），不是真正的 L3 partitioning。\"1 hour\" 工时正确，**收益 +2-5%**（pinning 避 E-core 抢占，不是 cache 隔离）。\n\n## 6. AMO aggregation 核实\n\n**transcript 里不存在这一条**。CP-SAT 内部 presolve 已经自动做 MaxClique→at_most_one 合并（[primer](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/)），用户层无干预空间。可能是路线图作者把 transcript §4 worker matrix 里的 `boolean_encoding_level` 误归类为\"AMO aggregation\"。**这一项应剔除或重命名**为 \"boolean_encoding_level / linearization_level worker tuning\"，独立收益 ~1-3%（Phase 3B 已经在调）。\n\n## 7. combined 加和合理性\n\nDouble-count 风险**显著**：THP（reduce TLB miss）、malloc（reduce alloc latency + fragmentation）、PGO（code layout, I-cache）、L3 isolation（D-cache contention）—— 前三都改善内存子系统。SAT solver \"60-70% 等内存\" 是 ceiling：理论上界 ~60%，但同一份 stall 不能被 4 个干预各削一遍。经验上 stack efficiency ~0.5-0.7。简单加和：THP 15% + malloc 7% + PGO 5% + pinning 3% = 30% → 真实 (1.15×1.07×1.05×1.03)−1 ≈ 33% 上界，乘 0.6 stack efficiency ≈ **+20%**，落在 claim 区间下沿。\n\n## verdict\n\n**GO-WITH-CAVEATS**\n\n值得做（按 ROI 序）：(1) THP madvise — 1 行 `transparent_hugepage=madvise`，**+10-25%**，几乎免费；(2) jemalloc LD_PRELOAD — env var 一行，**+5-10%**；(3) cpuset P-core pinning — `systemd-run --scope`，**+2-5%**，1h；(4) PGO — 真正成本 5-7 天，收益 **+3-7%**，最末做。\n\n剔除：**AMO aggregation 整项移除**（transcript 无源、CP-SAT 自动 presolve）；**L3 CAT** 改名 cpuset pinning（13th gen 不支持 CAT）。\n\n修正后 combined gain：**+15-22%**（不是 15-30%），仍是高 ROI 包。修正后工时：THP+malloc+pinning ~3h；PGO 仍是 5-7 天大头。**前 3 项立刻做（一上午搞定 90% 收益），PGO 单独提 ROI 评估，可能 P2 而不是 P1**。\n\nSources:\n- [OR-Tools PGO discussion #4012](https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/4012)\n- [Towards Faster Reasoners by Using THP (Springer 2020)](https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-58475-7_18)\n- [Intel CMT-CAT issue #249 - 13th gen i9](https://github.com/intel/intel-cmt-cat/issues/249)\n- [jemalloc/tcmalloc benchmark HN](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=17457699)\n- Transcript: `/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd/docs/research/agent_transcripts/ae3590b7e2f938057.output` line 52\n- Roadmap entry: `/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd/docs/phase3c_optimization_roadmap_v1.md:58`"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":207,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2089,"cache_read_input_tokens":41598,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2089,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CasSE1cgx5kTKCha2Qe2v","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"cfbd5657-8481-44c5-8689-6fd805550256","timestamp":"2026-05-09T18:04:32.030Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
